Option B — if runway = 30 months (implied burn ≈ $40K/mo)
"With $1.2M cash and a reported 30-month runway, Summit is operating at an implied net cash burn of ~$40K/month while generating $2.4M in revenue last quarter (~$800K/month). This indicates strong operating leverage: revenue covers ongoing cash needs by a wide margin. The 30-month runway provides substantial cushion for executing our growth initiatives, though we should confirm working-capital timing and any one-off items that affect reported cash."

