“We have $1.2M in cash and a current net cash burn of ~$72K/month, providing approximately 16.7 months of runway at today’s operating pace. This gives us sufficient near-term runway to execute our product milestones, while we prioritize converting revenue to cash and reducing discretionary spend to extend runway further.”

Expanded paragraph (for board/finance deck)
“Cash position: $1.2M. Operating cash usage: ~$72K/month net. Runway: ~16.7 months. Revenue last quarter was $2.4M, but our current cash burn figure is net of operating cash receipts and payments — primary risks to this runway are increased hiring and marketing spend, and collection of accounts receivable. Key mitigants include tightening hiring, prioritizing high-margin deals, and accelerating collections. We recommend maintaining a 12–13 week cash forecast and preparing a downside plan targeting 6–9 months of runway if revenue cadence deteriorates.”

